---
description: Project rules for the Kubernetes FinOps Agent
alwaysApply: true
---
- Stack: Python 3.11+, FastAPI + Pydantic backend in `backend/app`, React + TypeScript + Vite in `frontend/`.
- Shared contract lives in `backend/app/models/schemas.py`. NEVER rename/remove fields there without telling the other developer.
- Units: CPU = integer millicores, memory = integer MiB, timestamps = ISO-8601 with timezone.
- Optimizer and critic are deterministic Python. An LLM (NVIDIA NIM) may only phrase explanations, never decide.
- Requests only: never propose or change limits. Nothing may call kubectl or write to a cluster. YAML patches are review-only.
- Missing/insufficient data must produce a conservative status, never an optimistic guess.
- Tests must pass an explicit clock (`now`); never depend on today's date.
- Write pytest tests with every module; run `pytest -q` before finishing.
- Do not invent Zetaris/Meterless endpoints; leave a TODO and a local fallback.
- Developer 1 owns: data_loader.py, optimizer_service.py, data/*. Developer 2 owns: critic, orchestrator, report, api routes, frontend.
